  "_exec_summary": [
    {
      "ESSeqNum": 0,
      "FacilityID": 1000118703,
      "SummaryText": "This process consists of receiving, storing, and shipping of ISO Containers (UN Portable Tank type T14) containing 70% Hydrofluoric acid solution. \n\nIn this phase of the risk analysis,  as a most probable scenario that we have analyzed is a damage to the relief valve and rupture of the membrane inside the valve. Under this scenario, we expect to have the relief valve changed within an hour.  Using the Aloha program, we estimate about 0.054 lb of vapor release from evaporation with the \"Threat point\" being within 5 ft. Using the SCBA and all other appropriate PPE, the valve will be replaced and any spill will be collected and neutralized. \n\nThis RMP will be updated when the facility construction is complete and when the mixing of this chemical to produce lesser concentration HF product and other mixes begins."
    }
  ]
